WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.419
It was not a pleasant sight.

2
00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:05.630
Everywhere people were arguing and fighting.

3
00:00:05.631 --> 00:00:07.809
Some were even crying.

4
00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:12.069
Aunt Martha and Mrs. Jenkins would not look at each other.

5
00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:16.276
"Don't you have anything nice to say to each other?" Panther asked.

6
00:00:16.277 --> 00:00:21.040
Both women stubbornly shook their heads.

7
00:00:21.041 --> 00:00:24.218
Bobby and Cy got into another argument.

8
00:00:24.219 --> 00:00:27.309
"You act like a baby," Cy said.

9
00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:31.095
"You're too bossy," Bobby said in return.

10
00:00:31.096 --> 00:00:34.047
Meanwhile Jane was speaking with Mr. Keefer.

11
00:00:34.048 --> 00:00:38.722
"My favorite candy is red cherry," she said.

12
00:00:38.723 --> 00:00:42.889
"I think you eat too many sweets," the shop owner said.

13
00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:47.474
"I don't eat as much as Bobby," she loudly replied.

14
00:00:47.475 --> 00:00:49.726
"That's why he's so fat."

15
00:00:49.727 --> 00:00:52.510
Panther could not take it anymore!

16
00:00:52.511 --> 00:00:57.813
"Doesn't anyone have a nice word to say?" she shouted.

17
00:00:57.814 --> 00:01:00.551
For a second, people stopped talking.

18
00:01:00.552 --> 00:01:03.077
They all stared at Panther.

19
00:01:03.078 --> 00:01:09.606
"My, your voice certainly is loud," Mrs. Jenkins said nastily.

20
00:01:09.607 --> 00:01:13.654
"You're very rude," said a man, frowning.

21
00:01:13.655 --> 00:01:16.466
Panther wanted to crawl under a rock.

22
00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:19.553
Everything was her fault.

23
00:01:19.554 --> 00:01:23.071
"Pan-ter," Lamb cooed.

24
00:01:23.072 --> 00:01:25.466
He reached out his chubby arms.

25
00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:28.123
Panther took him from Aunt Martha.

26
00:01:28.124 --> 00:01:30.541
Lamb giggled and smiled.

27
00:01:30.542 --> 00:01:33.999
Panther looked into his eyes for a long time.

28
00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.595
"There's nothing bad about you, Lamb," she said softly.

29
00:01:38.596 --> 00:01:43.367
Looking around, she added, "I wish we could all be like you."

30
00:01:43.368 --> 00:01:46.185
Panther thought about what she had just said.

31
00:01:46.186 --> 00:01:50.618
"You only think good things about people," she said to Lamb.

32
00:01:50.619 --> 00:01:52.608
That gave her an idea.

33
00:01:52.609 --> 00:01:55.560
"Aunt Martha," she said suddenly.

34
00:01:55.561 --> 00:01:59.750
"What is it, child?" Aunt Martha asked sharply.

35
00:01:59.751 --> 00:02:03.807
"Thank you for being so kind to us," Panther said.

36
00:02:03.808 --> 00:02:06.928
She thought about how she really felt.

37
00:02:06.929 --> 00:02:10.981
"We know it's not easy to look after us," she continued.

38
00:02:10.982 --> 00:02:13.207
"So we really appreciate it."

39
00:02:13.208 --> 00:02:18.619
"Well, you children can be annoying," Aunt Martha said truthfully.

40
00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:21.672
"But at least you have good manners."

41
00:02:21.673 --> 00:02:24.688
Panther went over to Cy and Bobby.

42
00:02:24.689 --> 00:02:28.421
"Don't you have anything nice to say?" she asked her brothers.

43
00:02:28.422 --> 00:02:31.993
Bobby crossed his arms stubbornly and shook his head.

44
00:02:31.994 --> 00:02:34.597
Cy turned his head and ignored him.

45
00:02:34.598 --> 00:02:38.333
"Look into your hearts," she said to her siblings.

46
00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:42.144
"I'm sure you'll find good things, not just bad."

47
00:02:42.145 --> 00:02:44.503
The children looked at each other.

48
00:02:44.504 --> 00:02:47.036
Bobby stuck his tongue out at Cy.

49
00:02:47.037 --> 00:02:49.268
Panther sighed loudly and said:

50
00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:52.338
"People should say what they think.

51
00:02:52.339 --> 00:02:55.480
But what if we thought only nice things?"

52
00:02:55.481 --> 00:02:58.914
Some of the townspeople stopped to listen to Panther.

53
00:02:58.915 --> 00:03:03.181
"Being honest doesn't mean being nasty," she continued.

54
00:03:03.182 --> 00:03:05.415
Bobby glanced at Cy.

55
00:03:05.416 --> 00:03:07.988
Cy gave him a quick smile.

56
00:03:07.989 --> 00:03:12.698
"And sometimes, words may not even be necessary," Panther said.

57
00:03:12.699 --> 00:03:16.951
"But if you have to say something, then try to say something kind."

58
00:03:16.952 --> 00:03:21.775
"Well, Cy is a big bully," said Bobby.

59
00:03:21.776 --> 00:03:24.796
"But sometimes he's cool."

60
00:03:24.797 --> 00:03:30.953
"Even though Bobby is fat," giggled Jane, "he's funny."

61
00:03:30.954 --> 00:03:33.196
Bobby's face turned red.

62
00:03:33.197 --> 00:03:36.078
"I'm not fat!" he yelled.

63
00:03:36.079 --> 00:03:38.852
Cy quickly interrupted his siblings.

64
00:03:38.853 --> 00:03:41.439
"Panther is right," he said.

65
00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.712
"We can be truthful in a nice way. Right, Jane?"

66
00:03:45.713 --> 00:03:48.809
Jane was still giggling but she nodded.

67
00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:51.343
Lamb gave Panther a big hug.

68
00:03:51.344 --> 00:03:53.190
She held him tightly.

69
00:03:53.191 --> 00:03:55.876
Then Aunt Martha took Lamb from Panther.

70
00:03:55.877 --> 00:04:00.411
"All right, children," she said, "let's get home."

71
00:04:00.412 --> 00:04:04.438
As she passed Mrs. Jenkins, she paused and smiled.

72
00:04:04.439 --> 00:04:06.826
Mrs. Jenkins smiled back.

73
00:04:06.827 --> 00:04:09.409
Other people also stopped arguing.

74
00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:12.849
Some even started to laugh again.

75
00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:17.033
When they got home, the children sat outside on the porch.

76
00:04:17.034 --> 00:04:19.574
The sun was still shining brightly.

77
00:04:19.575 --> 00:04:23.562
"How do you think this wish will end?" asked Bobby.

78
00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:26.881
"Just as Panther wished," said Cy.

79
00:04:26.882 --> 00:04:29.494
"We'll speak what's on our mind."

80
00:04:29.495 --> 00:04:33.972
"But we'll be thinking only nice thoughts," said Jane.

81
00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:37.336
"At least we'll try to," said Bobby.

82
00:04:37.337 --> 00:04:40.875
He was still upset that Jane had called him fat.

83
00:04:40.876 --> 00:04:43.578
The Barth children sat close together.

84
00:04:43.579 --> 00:04:48.227
"I'm so lucky to have you," Panther said to her siblings.

85
00:04:48.228 --> 00:04:52.991
"And that's truly from my heart."

